---
// This standalone internal page avoids public layouts so experiments cannot affect production navigation or routing.
import '../../../styles/global.css';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>AMARA Design Lab</title>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-surface font-body text-on-surface antialiased">
    <div class="min-h-screen bg-surface">
      <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[1120px] px-6 py-16 md:px-12 md:py-24">
        <header class="max-w-4xl border-b border-outline-variant pb-16 md:pb-20">
          <p class="am-text-caption am-text-caption--upper mb-6 text-primary">
            Internal tool · Visual experimentation
          </p>
          <h1 class="am-display-xl">AMARA Design Lab</h1>
          <p class="am-text-subtitle mt-8 max-w-3xl text-on-surface-variant">
            This is a controlled internal space for testing new visual directions before they become part of the public AMARA system.
          </p>
        </header>

        <section class="py-16 md:py-20" aria-labelledby="design-lab-principles">
          <h2 id="design-lab-principles" class="am-text-title mb-10">Working principles</h2>

          <div class="border-y border-outline-variant divide-y divide-outline-variant">
            <article class="grid gap-4 py-8 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.35fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] md:gap-12">
              <h3 class="am-text-subtitle text-on-surface">Explore safely</h3>
              <p class="am-text-body max-w-2xl text-on-surface-variant">
                New ideas are tested here first while public pages remain unchanged.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="grid gap-4 py-8 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.35fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] md:gap-12">
              <h3 class="am-text-subtitle text-on-surface">Compare clearly</h3>
              <p class="am-text-body max-w-2xl text-on-surface-variant">
                Experiments should make typography, rhythm, imagery, hierarchy and composition easy to compare.
              </p>
            </article>

            <article class="grid gap-4 py-8 md:grid-cols-[minmax(0,0.35fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] md:gap-12">
              <h3 class="am-text-subtitle text-on-surface">Promote deliberately</h3>
              <p class="am-text-body max-w-2xl text-on-surface-variant">
                A successful experiment only becomes part of the real AMARA system after explicit approval and a separate implementation task.
              </p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- The index remains visually neutral; experimental composition belongs on separate Design Lab pages. -->
        <section class="max-w-4xl border-t border-outline-variant pt-16 md:pt-20" aria-labelledby="design-lab-experiments">
          <p class="am-text-caption am-text-caption--upper mb-5 text-muted">Experiments</p>
          <h2 id="design-lab-experiments" class="am-text-title">No active design test yet.</h2>
          <p class="am-text-body mt-6 max-w-3xl text-on-surface-variant">
            The first planned study is a contemporary interpretation of the AMARA homepage. It will later be created as a separate Design Lab page without modifying the current homepage.
          </p>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
